    {
      "qid": 7,
      "questionUid": "sha256:d634108ff68b961a5b9c98ecc395f8264d93eaa96b30c5a5d9cd952166e90859|7",
      "sourceOrdinal": 7,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "④",
      "decisiveCalculation": "The source graph has f'>0 before x=−2 and f'<0 on (−2,1), then f'>0 after x=1. The isolated zeros x=0 and x=2 do not change sign. Thus a=−2 is a local maximum and b=1 a local minimum; a+b=−1 (④)."
    },
    {
      "qid": 8,
      "questionUid": "sha256:d634108ff68b961a5b9c98ecc395f8264d93eaa96b30c5a5d9cd952166e90859|8",
      "sourceOrdinal": 8,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "③",
      "decisiveCalculation": "f'(2)=4+a=6, so a=2. From f(2)=3, 4+2a+b=3 gives b=−5; a+b=−3 (③)."
    },
    {
      "qid": 9,
      "questionUid": "sha256:d634108ff68b961a5b9c98ecc395f8264d93eaa96b30c5a5d9cd952166e90859|9",
      "sourceOrdinal": 9,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "①",
      "decisiveCalculation": "The odd term integrates to 0 and ∫_-a^a4dx=8a=16, so a=2 (①)."
    },
    {
      "qid": 10,
      "questionUid": "sha256:d634108ff68b961a5b9c98ecc395f8264d93eaa96b30c5a5d9cd952166e90859|10",
      "sourceOrdinal": 10,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "④",
      "decisiveCalculation": "f'=3(x−3)(x+1), so the local maximum occurs at x=−1. f(−1)=5+a=12 gives a=7; f(3)=−20 (④)."
    },
    {
      "qid": 11,
      "questionUid": "sha256:d634108ff68b961a5b9c98ecc395f8264d93eaa96b30c5a5d9cd952166e90859|11",
      "sourceOrdinal": 11,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "②",
      "decisiveCalculation": "For monotonicity on R, 3x²+2x−a≥0 for every x. Its discriminant 4+12a≤0, hence a≤−1/3, with maximum −1/3 (②)."
    },
    {
      "qid": 12,
      "questionUid": "sha256:d634108ff68b961a5b9c98ecc395f8264d93eaa96b30c5a5d9cd952166e90859|12",
      "sourceOrdinal": 12,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "②",
      "decisiveCalculation": "The source graph is below the axis on [−3,1] and above on [1,4], so ∫_-3^4 f=−A+B=−3+2=−1. ∫_-3^4 2x dx=16−9=7; total 6 (②)."
    },
    {
      "qid": 13,
      "questionUid": "sha256:d634108ff68b961a5b9c98ecc395f8264d93eaa96b30c5a5d9cd952166e90859|13",
      "sourceOrdinal": 13,
      "disposition": "ITEM_HOLD",
      "answer": null,
      "decisiveCalculation": "For f=x³−12x−1, f'(x)=3(x²−4); local maximum f(−2)=15 and local minimum f(2)=−17. For the listed a values 14,15,16,17,18, the distinct counts for |f|=a are respectively 6,5,4,2,2. None gives exactly 3, so this qid is ITEM_HOLD; no source repair inferred."
    },
    {
      "qid": 14,
      "questionUid": "sha256:d634108ff68b961a5b9c98ecc395f8264d93eaa96b30c5a5d9cd952166e90859|14",
      "sourceOrdinal": 14,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "③",
      "decisiveCalculation": "If x is the corner cut, V=x(12−2x)², 0<x<6. V'=(12−2x)(12−6x), so V increases to x=2 then decreases; V(2)=2·8²=128 (③)."
    },
    {
      "qid": 15,
      "questionUid": "sha256:d634108ff68b961a5b9c98ecc395f8264d93eaa96b30c5a5d9cd952166e90859|15",
      "sourceOrdinal": 15,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "①",
      "decisiveCalculation": "f−g=x³−x²−x+6−a. φ'=3x²−2x−1=(3x+1)(x−1); on x≥0 the minimum is φ(1)=5. Thus the maximum possible a is 5 (①)."
    },
    {
      "qid": 16,
      "questionUid": "sha256:d634108ff68b961a5b9c98ecc395f8264d93eaa96b30c5a5d9cd952166e90859|16",
      "sourceOrdinal": 16,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "⑤",
      "decisiveCalculation": "The integrand is ((x²+x)f(x))'. The boundary value is 6f(2)−2f(1)=6(2−a) because f(1)=0. Set 6(2−a)=−12 to get a=4. Then f=x²−5x+4 and ∫_1^4 f=−9/2 (⑤)."
    },
    {
      "qid": 17,
      "questionUid": "sha256:d634108ff68b961a5b9c98ecc395f8264d93eaa96b30c5a5d9cd952166e90859|17",
      "sourceOrdinal": 17,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "①",
      "decisiveCalculation": "Let h(x)=x³−3x; its local maximum/minimum are 2 at −1 and −2 at 1. For n=1,2,3 the level 2−n is inside (−2,2), giving 3 roots each; n=4 gives 2 roots; n=5,…,10 each gives 1. Sum=9+2+6=17 (①)."
    },
    {
      "qid": 18,
      "questionUid": "sha256:d634108ff68b961a5b9c98ecc395f8264d93eaa96b30c5a5d9cd952166e90859|18",
      "sourceOrdinal": 18,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "②",
      "decisiveCalculation": "On [0,1], f≤0, so S₁=∫₀¹(x−x³)dx=1/4. S₂=∫₁ᵃ(x³−x)dx=a⁴/4−a²/2+1/4. Setting S₂=4S₁=1 gives (a²−3)(a²+1)=0; a>1 gives √3 (②)."
    },
    {
      "qid": 19,
      "questionUid": "sha256:d634108ff68b961a5b9c98ecc395f8264d93eaa96b30c5a5d9cd952166e90859|19",
      "sourceOrdinal": 19,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "③",
      "decisiveCalculation": "f≤0 on (−1,0) and f≥0 on (0,1). F(−1)=−∫_-1^1f=4/3, so (가) true. F decreases to F(0)=−7/3 then increases, so (나) false. For −1≤x≤1, F(x)=3x²−(2/3)x³−7/3; its integral from −1 to1 is −8/3, so (다) true. Only (가),(다): ③."
    },
    {
      "qid": 20,
      "questionUid": "sha256:d634108ff68b961a5b9c98ecc395f8264d93eaa96b30c5a5d9cd952166e90859|20",
      "sourceOrdinal": 20,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "⑤",
      "decisiveCalculation": "For m>2, x_A=m³/120 and x_B=a(m−2)²/2. Equal speeds give m²/40=a(m−2). Substitution into equal positions gives m/120=(m−2)/80, hence m=6 and a=9/40. Thus 40(a+m)=249 (⑤)."
    },
    {
      "qid": 21,
      "questionUid": "sha256:d634108ff68b961a5b9c98ecc395f8264d93eaa96b30c5a5d9cd952166e90859|21",
      "sourceOrdinal": 21,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "①",
      "decisiveCalculation": "Oddness gives ∫_-3^3 f=0 and ∫₂⁵f=−∫_-5^-2f=20. Also ∫₂³f=∫_-2³f=6, hence ∫₃⁵f=14. The polynomial part ∫_-3^5 4x dx=32, total 46 (①)."
    },
    {
      "qid": 22,
      "questionUid": "sha256:d634108ff68b961a5b9c98ecc395f8264d93eaa96b30c5a5d9cd952166e90859|서술형1",
      "sourceOrdinal": 22,
      "disposition": "RESOLVED",
      "answer": "$11$",
      "decisiveCalculation": "Differentiate the identity: f(x)=4x−8. Setting x=a in the original gives 2a²−8a+6=0, so a=1 or 3; a>1 selects 3. Then f(4)+a=8+3=11."
    },
    {
      "qid": 23,
      "questionUid": "sha256:d634108ff68b961a5b9c98ecc395f8264d93eaa96b30c5a5d9cd952166e90859|서술형2",
      "sourceOrdinal": 23,
